{
  "uid": "hydra-red",
  "title": "Hydra \u2014 RED (rate, errors, duration)",
  "tags": [
    "hydra-lab",
    "red"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this board",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Rate / Errors / Duration, per service.**\n\n**429s are plotted separately from 5xx and always will be (FR-079, D11).** A throttled request is the rate limiter doing its job; a 5xx is the service failing. Summing them into one 'error rate' hides a working control behind a fake outage \u2014 and hides a real outage behind a busy afternoon. The benchmark report keeps the same split.\n\nAll application metrics here come from the OpenTelemetry Java agent. Neither service has a metrics endpoint of its own \u2014 there is no Micrometer registry in either one."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Request rate (RPS)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The R in RED. Requests per second per service, from the agent's HTTP server instrumentation."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Errors: 5xx (service failures)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{http_response_status_code=~\"5..\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "5xx {{service}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Genuine server-side failures. Deliberately does NOT include 429 \u2014 see the panel to the right."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Throttled: 429 (rate limiter working)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{http_response_status_code=\"429\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "429 {{service}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "FR-079 / D11. A 429 means the limiter rejected a request as designed. It is NOT an error and is never counted as one. Fails closed on a Redis outage, so a spike here can also mean the cache is gone \u2014 see the cache-down drill."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Duration p50 / p95 / p99",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le, service) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50 {{service}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, service) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{service}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, service) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{service}}",
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The D in RED. Quantiles from the agent's histogram; read p99 next to the GC panel on the runtime board before blaming the application."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Status codes",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (http_response_status_code) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{http_response_status_code}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Every status, unaggregated. The panel to check first when the 5xx and 429 panels disagree with intuition."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Requests by route",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (http_route, service) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}} {{http_route}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    }
  ]
}
